<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM - Some corn basis bids drop.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM - Some corn basis bids drop.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Several Midwest grain dealers reduced corn basis bids in reaction to weak values at the U.S. Gulf, dealers said.</p>
<p>Kansas City corn was bid four cents per bushel over the CBOT March versus six over Thursday, and Laredo, Texas, corn was bid 60 cents over versus 64 over Thursday.</p>
<p>Other markets were quiet, with some dealers reporting a small amount of corn and soybean movement.</p>
<p>Corn CIF basis offers were down one to three cents early Friday from Thursday, while basis bids were mostly unchanged.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
